<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>PQC Readiness Report — {{ generated_at }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #ffffff; --fg: #1a1a1a; --muted: #5b6472; --border: #e2e5ea;
    --critical: #b3261e; --high: #b5560a; --medium: #8a6d00; --low: #2e6b3f;
    --card: #f7f8fa; --accent: #2454a6;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root { --bg:#14161a; --fg:#e8eaed; --muted:#9aa3b2; --card:#1e2126; --border:#2b2f36; --accent:#7ba7ff; }
  }
  body { font-family: -apple-system, Segoe UI, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; background:var(--bg); color:var(--fg); max-width: 980px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; line-height:1.5; }
  h1 { margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .summary-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(140px,1fr)); gap: 0.75rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .stat { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; }
  .stat .n { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .stat .l { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.03em; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0 2rem; font-size: 0.88rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: var(--card); }
  .overflow { overflow-x: auto; }
  tr.tier-Critical td:nth-child(1) { border-left: 4px solid var(--critical); }
  tr.tier-High td:nth-child(1) { border-left: 4px solid var(--high); }
  tr.tier-Medium td:nth-child(1) { border-left: 4px solid var(--medium); }
  tr.tier-Low td:nth-child(1) { border-left: 4px solid var(--low); }
  .badge { display:inline-block; padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .badge.vulnerable { background:#fbdedb; color:var(--critical); }
  .badge.weakened { background:#fbe8c9; color:var(--medium); }
  .badge.safe { background:#dcf3e3; color:var(--low); }
  .badge.pqc { background:#dbe8fb; color:var(--accent); }
  .badge.unknown { background:#e7e7e7; color:#555; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .badge.vulnerable { background:#3a1f1e; color:#ff8a80; }
    .badge.weakened { background:#3a2f14; color:#ffcc66; }
    .badge.safe { background:#173a24; color:#7de3a0; }
    .badge.pqc { background:#182a45; color:#9dc0ff; }
    .badge.unknown { background:#2b2f36; color:#aab; }
  }
  section { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  .timeline li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  footer { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 1rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) Readiness Report</h1>
<div class="meta">Generated {{ generated_at }} &middot; {{ summary.total_assets }} asset(s) scanned &middot; threat horizon assumption: {{ threat_horizon_years }} years</div>

<section>
  <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
  <p>This report assesses network-facing TLS/certificate cryptography against post-quantum risk.
     It does <strong>not</strong> test whether an attacker can break these systems today — it tests whether
     the cryptography in use today will still protect this traffic once a cryptographically relevant
     quantum computer (CRQC) exists, and whether traffic captured today could be decrypted retroactively
     ("harvest now, decrypt later").</p>
  <div class="summary-grid">
    <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ summary.total_findings }}</div><div class="l">Findings</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ summary.vulnerable_count }}</div><div class="l">Vulnerable</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ summary.weakened_count }}</div><div class="l">Weakened</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ summary.safe_count }}</div><div class="l">Safe</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ summary.pqc_count }}</div><div class="l">Post-Quantum</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ summary.critical_count }}</div><div class="l">Critical Priority</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ summary.high_count }}</div><div class="l">High Priority</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ summary.internet_facing_hndl_count }}</div><div class="l">Internet-Facing HNDL Risk</div></div>
  </div>
  {% if scan_errors %}
  <h3>Scan Errors</h3>
  <div class="overflow"><table><tr><th>Asset</th><th>Reason</th></tr>
  {%- for e in scan_errors %}<tr><td>{{ e.target }}</td><td>{{ e.reason }}</td></tr>{%- endfor %}
  </table></div>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Crypto Inventory Findings</h2>
  <p>Every distinct algorithm observed, doing every distinct job (key exchange, certificate signature,
     or symmetric cipher), across every scanned asset.</p>
  <div class="overflow">
  <table>
    <tr><th>Asset</th><th>Protocol</th><th>Mechanism</th><th>Algorithm</th><th>Key Size</th><th>Expiry</th><th>Quantum-Vulnerable</th><th>Classification</th></tr>
    {%- for row in findings_table %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ row.asset }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.protocol_version or "—" }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.mechanism }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.algorithm }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.key_size or "—" }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.expiry or "—" }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.quantum_vulnerable }}</td>
      <td><span class="badge {{ row.classification|lower }}">{{ row.classification }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Prioritized Remediation Roadmap</h2>
  <p>Findings are ranked by a priority score combining: crypto severity, whether "harvest now, decrypt
     later" applies and how far the asset's declared data retention extends past the assumed quantum
     threat horizon, internet vs. internal exposure, and remediation complexity. Full methodology in the
     README.</p>
  {% for tier in ["Critical", "High", "Medium", "Low"] %}
  {%- if roadmap[tier] %}
  <h3>{{ tier }} Priority</h3>
  <div class="overflow">
  <table>
    <tr><th>Asset</th><th>Protocol</th><th>Algorithm</th><th>Issue</th><th>Why It Matters</th><th>Recommended Fix</th><th>Effort</th><th>Exposure</th><th>Retention</th></tr>
    {%- for row in roadmap[tier] %}
    <tr class="tier-{{ tier }}">
      <td>{{ row.asset }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.protocol_version or "—" }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.algorithm }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.classification }} ({{ row.quantum_attack }})</td>
      <td>{{ row.rationale }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.recommended_replacement }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.remediation_complexity }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.exposure }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.retention_years }}y</td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
  {%- if not (roadmap["Critical"] or roadmap["High"] or roadmap["Medium"] or roadmap["Low"]) %}
  <p>No outstanding remediation items — every observed algorithm is already Safe or Post-Quantum.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="migration-timeline">Migration Timeline (NIST / CNSA 2.0 Anchors)</h2>
  <p>This assessment's urgency framing is anchored to public federal guidance, not an arbitrary internal deadline:</p>
  <ul class="timeline">
    {%- for milestone in timeline %}
    <li><strong>{{ milestone.date }}</strong> — {{ milestone.description }}</li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  <p><em>Sources: NIST IR 8547 (Transition to Post-Quantum Cryptography Standards),
     NSA CNSA 2.0 Transition Timeline (CSA, 2022, reaffirmed 2025), OMB M-26-15,
     National Security Memorandum 10.</em></p>
</section>

<footer>
  Scope: network-facing TLS/X.509 only (data-at-rest, VPN/IPsec, SSH, and HSM-embedded keys are out of
  scope for v1). Classification logic is rule-based and fully editable — see
  <code>pqc_audit/rules.yaml</code>. Detection limitation: this scan reports the classical/hybrid key
  exchange actually negotiated by the scanning client; a server that only offers a PQC hybrid to clients
  that request it may show as classical here even if partially PQC-ready.
</footer>

</body>
</html>
